 place was very close. “Sans Atout” from Sweden was second in the first round and fourth in the second, achieving three points. “Lucky Girl” from Finland finished fifth and second, getting the same number of points. The Finnish boat “Örn” came in on third place twice, and finished a thankless overall fourth place with two points. In the sail-off for the silver medal, “Sans Atout” won by almost one minute, after a fierce struggle, with the lead alternating a few times."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Race #1"] [:th {} "Race #2"] [:th {} "Match Race for 2/3"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Taifun"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]] [:td {} "14"] [:td {} "2-15:59 (1)"] [:td {} "2-12:59 (1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "12"} [:a {:href "/athletes/62141"} "Thoralf Glad"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/64256"} "Valentin Aass"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/61447"} "Andreas Brecke"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/61672"} "Torleiv Corneliussen"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/62478"} "Christian Jebe"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Sans Atout"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "3"] [:td {} "2-16:40 (2)"] [:td {} "2-16:04 (4)"] [:td {} "2-26:44 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "12"} [:a {:href "/athletes/62337"} "Bengt Heyman"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/62325"} "Emil Henriques"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/64143"} "Herbert W